('space-8x1','space','young','medium','Why does the Moon appear to change shape during the month?','["We see different portions of its sunlit half","The Moon changes its actual shape","Earth covers it every night","Its light switches on and off"]'::jsonb,0,'The Moon keeps roughly the same shape, but its position changes how much of its sunlit side we see.','',''),
('space-8x2','space','young','medium','Why is a year on Mars longer than a year on Earth?','["Mars takes longer to orbit the Sun","Mars rotates faster","Mars has more moons","Mars has a thicker atmosphere"]'::jsonb,0,'A year is the time needed to orbit the Sun, and Mars has a longer orbit.','',''),
('space-8x3','space','young','medium','What causes a solar eclipse?','["The Moon passes between Earth and the Sun","Earth passes between the Moon and Sun","The Sun passes between Earth and Moon","Mars blocks sunlight"]'::jsonb,0,'A solar eclipse occurs when the Moon moves between Earth and the Sun.','',''),
('space-8x4','space','young','medium','Why do astronauts appear weightless while orbiting Earth?','["They and their spacecraft are in continuous free fall around Earth","There is no gravity in space","Their suits remove gravity","The Moon pulls them upward"]'::jsonb,0,'Astronauts in orbit are continuously falling around Earth, creating the sensation of weightlessness.','',''),
('space-8x5','space','young','medium','Which planet has the most prominent ring system?','["Saturn","Earth","Mars","Mercury"]'::jsonb,0,'Saturn is famous for its extensive and bright ring system.','',''),
