('world-explorer-8-difficult-1','world','old','difficult','A mountain range lies between a moist ocean and a dry interior. Why might the interior receive less rainfall?','["Air rises and loses moisture on the windward side, leaving drier descending air on the other side","Mountains absorb all rainfall permanently","Dry air cannot cross the equator","The ocean stops evaporating"]'::jsonb,0,'This is the rain-shadow effect.','',''),
('world-explorer-8-difficult-2','world','old','difficult','Two cities have the same latitude but very different average temperatures. Which factor could best explain this?','["Altitude, ocean currents or distance from large water bodies","Their names","Their time zones alone","The number of roads"]'::jsonb,0,'Latitude is important, but altitude, currents and continentality also affect climate.','',''),
('world-explorer-8-difficult-3','world','old','difficult','Why does longitude matter when determining local solar time?','["Earth rotates through 360° of longitude, so different longitudes face the Sun at different times","Longitude measures height above sea level","Longitude controls rainfall directly","Longitude is the same as latitude"]'::jsonb,0,'Earth’s rotation creates differences in local solar time with longitude.','',''),
('world-explorer-8-difficult-4','world','old','difficult','A map has a scale of 1 cm = 20 km. Two towns are 7.5 cm apart on the map. What is their approximate real distance?','["150 km","75 km","135 km","175 km"]'::jsonb,0,'7.5 × 20 = 150 km.','',''),
('world-explorer-8-difficult-5','world','old','difficult','Why are densely populated settlements often found near major rivers even though floods can be dangerous?','["Rivers provide water, fertile land, transport and other resources","Rivers prevent all disease","Rivers make mountains disappear","Rivers guarantee no flooding"]'::jsonb,0,'Rivers have historically supported agriculture, water supply and transport.','',''),
('world-explorer-8-difficult-6','world','old','difficult','If Earth had no axial tilt but continued orbiting the Sun, which major change would be expected?','["Seasonal differences caused by tilt would be greatly reduced","Day and night would disappear","Earth would stop rotating","The Moon would leave orbit"]'::jsonb,0,'Earth’s axial tilt is a major cause of seasonal variation.','',''),
('world-explorer-8-difficult-7','world','old','difficult','Why does a rain shadow usually form on the leeward side of a mountain?','["Air descends after losing much of its moisture on the windward side","Air gains all its moisture while descending","The leeward side is always at sea level","Mountains create water from rock"]'::jsonb,0,'Descending air warms and is often relatively dry after moisture loss.','',''),
('world-explorer-8-difficult-8','world','old','difficult','A river carries sediment from mountains toward the sea. What can happen when the river slows near its mouth?','["Sediment may be deposited, building a delta","All sediment turns into salt","The river becomes a mountain","Water stops evaporating"]'::jsonb,0,'Reduced flow speed can cause sediment deposition.','',''),
('world-explorer-8-difficult-9','world','old','difficult','Why can deforestation increase flood risk in some areas?','["Less vegetation can reduce interception and infiltration while increasing surface runoff","Trees always cause floods","Roots make all soil waterproof","Deforestation creates more rainfall everywhere"]'::jsonb,0,'Vegetation can slow runoff and help water infiltrate soils.','',''),
('world-explorer-8-difficult-10','world','old','difficult','Which evidence would best show that a region is becoming more urbanised?','["A growing share of people and land is concentrated in expanding towns and cities","More stars appear at night","The region changes latitude","Rivers stop flowing"]'::jsonb,0,'Urbanisation involves increasing concentration of population and development in urban areas.','',''),
('world-explorer-8-difficult-11','world','old','difficult','Why can ocean currents affect the climate of nearby coastlines?','["They transport heat and can warm or cool coastal air","They change the length of Earth’s day","They remove the atmosphere","They stop winds everywhere"]'::jsonb,0,'Currents redistribute heat through the ocean.','',''),
('world-explorer-8-difficult-12','world','old','difficult','A country stretches far from east to west. Why might it have several time zones?','["Different longitudes experience local noon at different times","Latitude changes every hour","Mountains create time zones","Climate determines clock time"]'::jsonb,0,'Large east-west distances span many longitudes.','',''),
('world-explorer-8-difficult-13','world','old','difficult','Why can a desert exist near a cold ocean current?','["Cold water can reduce evaporation and moisture available to the atmosphere","Cold currents always increase rainfall","Deserts cannot occur near oceans","Ocean currents create sand directly"]'::jsonb,0,'Cold currents can stabilize air and reduce evaporation, contributing to aridity in some coastal deserts.','',''),
('world-explorer-8-difficult-14','world','old','difficult','A population lives on a floodplain. Which action would reduce flood damage without moving everyone immediately?','["Use flood warnings, raised structures and protected evacuation routes","Remove all river vegetation","Build houses directly in the river channel","Block every drainage path"]'::jsonb,0,'Preparedness and flood-resilient infrastructure can reduce damage.','',''),
('world-explorer-8-difficult-15','world','old','difficult','Why do tectonic plate boundaries often have earthquakes?','["Movement and stress along plate boundaries can release stored energy suddenly","Plates are made of liquid water","Earthquakes happen only because of rainfall","Boundaries stop Earth from rotating"]'::jsonb,0,'Plate motion can build stress that is released as earthquakes.','',''),
